        ['Supporting documents (เอกสารประกอบการลงบัญชี)', 'The evidence an accounting entry refers to, such as the vendor\'s tax invoice, a transfer slip or a delivery note signed by the customer — must be kept for at least 5 years from the date the books are closed (Accounting Act B.E. 2543 (2000) s.14); in the system they can be attached as files to the document (the paperclip at the end of the row, or the Attachments section under the document)'],
        ['Freeze / cut-off', 'When a count starts, the system remembers the system quantity (freeze) and stops the goods in the count from moving in or out until it is posted — otherwise goods moving during the count would make the differences wrong'],
        ['Period close', 'Locking a month that has been checked, so nothing can be posted back into it'],
        ['Credit note (ใบลดหนี้)', 'The document the seller issues when it lowers the price or takes goods back after the tax invoice was issued (s.86/10); both sides use it to adjust output / input VAT'],
        ['Statement of financial position', 'A picture on one date: what the company owns (assets), whom it owes (liabilities) and how much belongs to the shareholders'],
        ['Income statement', 'Results over a period: revenue − cost of sales − expenses = profit'],
